+## S03 addendum (2026-09-30): the data16 branch law, hardware-proven
+
+Red-teaming the merged PR #690 verdict machinery (the encdiff
+canonicalisation and the DECLINED-DATA16 classification) went one level
+deeper than the audit and found that the "fixed-rel16 policy" the
+DECLINED-DATA16 verdict was documenting is not a policy at all in 64-bit
+mode — it is a hardware-invalid encoding.
+
+### The hardware experiments (Xeon, signal-based; raw exit codes of
+### no-libc binaries are mangled by this sandbox, so every verdict below
+### is a signal + RIP analysis, not an exit status)
+
+* `66 e8 00 00` (+2 following bytes): SIGSEGV, fault RIP = insn+6 +
+  disp32 read from 4 bytes past the opcode — the decoder consumed a
+  FULL 4-byte displacement. The 8-byte push width was measured the same
+  way (rsp delta −8 at the fault).
+* `66 0f 84 2c 01` (+200 zero bytes): 7-byte decode (dead 66 + 0f 84 +
+  disp32), fall-through landing +2 past the label, then `add %al,(%rax)`
+  on the padding faulted at NULL.
+* `66 e9 <rel32>` / `66 e8 <rel32>` / `66 0f 84 <rel32>` (the dead-prefix
+  rel32 rows): SIGILL at exactly the landing ud2, skipping the
+  fall-through ud2 — VALID encodings.
+* `66 eb 02` / `66 74 02` (dead-prefix SHORT rows): SIGILL at the landing
+  ud2 — VALID (and byte-identical to what GAS relaxes to).
+* `66 e2 02` with RCX=0x1_0000_0001: taken, RCX=0x1_0000_0000 at the
+  trap — the 66 is dead on the LOOP family in 64-bit mode (full RCX
+  counter). In 32-bit mode it is ALIVE (LOOPW counts CX), which the
+  encdiff canonicaliser now respects.
+
+So: in 64-bit mode the operand-size prefix is architecturally dead on
+near branches — `66 e9/e8/0f 8x` still consume the full 4-byte
+displacement. GAS 2.47 emits the truncated 2-byte-field rows anyway
+(`data16 jmp/je/call` with far or external targets, with
+R_X86_64_PC16): a GAS bug class whose objects mis-execute. lccc shared
+the worse version of it (rel16 rows for every target).
+
+### The fix
+
+The 64-bit encoder keeps the normal rel32 row; the central
+forced-data16 splice prepends the dead prefix; jmp/jcc register for
+relaxation like their plain siblings (JumpInfo::prefix66). Near targets
+shrink to `66 eb/7x rel8` — byte-identical to GAS. Far and external
+targets keep `66 e9/e8/0f 8x rel32` + R_X86_64_PLT32 — the shortest
+VALID encoding, a documented divergence from GAS's invalid bytes
+(tracked by encdiff's new ORACLE-INVALID verdict over
+tests/encdiff-corpus/data16-branches-64.insn). The 32-bit encoder keeps
+its real rel16 rows; the LOOP family keeps the prefix in both modes.
+
+### The second bug the new corpus exposed
+
+`jmp 1f+300` produced a relocation against a symbol literally named
+`1f+300` (undefined GLOBAL, raw architecture addend as the
+displacement): silently wrong code. Two half-fixes were required —
+resolve_numeric_name now rewrites addend-carrying numeric references to
+`.Lnum_N_K±C`, and the i686 add_relocation choke point now splits
+`symbol+constant` like the x86-64 one always has. Byte-exact GAS parity
+on jmp/je/call x 1f/1b x ±300 in both modes, zero leftover relocations.
+
+### encdiff classifier hardening (the audit's three findings, plus one)
+
+* callw/call are never unified (2-byte vs 4-byte return push); jmpw
+  unifies with jmp only in 32-bit mode; in 64-bit mode both render
+  hardware-invalid truncated rows and never unify.
+* Branch comparison carries BOTH invariants (absolute target AND
+  end-relative displacement) and matches on either — sound for backward
+  labels (fixed address) and forward ones (ride at a fixed distance from
+  the end); the end-relative-only comparison misjudged every backward
+  branch (short and near rows of ONE branch have different end-relative
+  displacements).
+* DECLINED-DATA16 is only claimable after round-trip verification;
+  failure escalates (WRONG-BYTES / UNVERIFIED-BYTES). The 32-bit LOOP
+  counter-width divergence gets its own documented-policy note.
+* ORACLE-INVALID partitions architecturally-invalid oracle bytes out of
+  the length race (and flags LCCC emitting them as WRONG-BYTES).
+
+### Measurements (Callgrind 3.24, Ir, old b205cf2c vs new)
+
+* branch-relaxation stress (3000 mixed branches): 352.0M -> 355.9M Ir
+  (+1.1%) — the prefix66 bookkeeping in the relaxer's edit loop.
+* data16 stress (2000 rows): 160.8M -> 186.7M Ir (+16.1%) — the new
+  rows now go through relaxation (the old path skipped it while emitting
+  invalid bytes); correctness work, not a regression to chase.
+* numeric-addend stress (2000 rows): 315.9M -> 263.7M Ir (−16.5%) — the
+  fold path is cheaper than the undefined-external-symbol machinery the
+  bug used to hit; the fix is also a performance win.
+* Real-corpus wall clock (branch+prefix casefiles, 3 runs): 29ms -> 30ms
+  (noise).
+
+Final corpus state: x86-64 12418 insns (BEATS=124 ok=12265
+ORACLE-INVALID=10 both-reject=19; zero bad verdicts; exit 0; −131B net);
+i686 833 insns (BEATS=6 ok=817 DECLINED-DATA16=7 both-reject=3; exit 0;
+−16B net). asm-diff whole-corpus green both modes (1418 + 672 groups vs
+GAS 2.47.20260726); full lib test suite 3890 tests green; rustfmt and
+clippy clean; 28 encdiff unit tests (was 11).
