+# architecturally dead on near branches in 64-bit mode, per the Intel
+# SDM operand-size rules; a 2-byte rel16 field desynchronises the
+# decoder and jumps through whatever follows). GAS 2.47 emits the
+# truncated `66 e9/e8/0f 8x rel16` for far targets and external
+# symbols (R_X86_64_PC16) — bytes that mis-execute on real hardware.
